<title>USA: U.S. ag exports rise 10 pct in fiscal 1996 - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. ag exports rise 10 pct in fiscal 1996 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of U.S. agricultural products rose by 10 percent during fiscal 1996 to total $59.8 billion, the Agriculture Department said Monday.</p>
<p>Here is USDA's list of exports by category:</p>
<p>--Live animals, $548 million, up six percent.</p>
<p>--Meat and poultry, $7.13 billion, up 14 percent.</p>
<p>--Dairy products and eggs, $929 million, up five percent.</p>
<p>--Animal fats, $675 million, down 20 percent.</p>
<p>--Hides and skins, $1.68 billion, down four percent.</p>
<p>--Wheat, $6.88 billion, up 39 percent.</p>
<p>--Rice, $1 billion, down four percent.</p>
<p>--Corn, $8.37 billion, up 26 percent.</p>
<p>--Other feed grains, $969 million, up 22 percent.</p>
<p>--Animal feeds, $3.99 billion, up nine percent.</p>
<p>--Soybeans, $6.3 billion, up 20 percent.</p>
<p>--Vegetable oils, $1.34 billion, down 30 percent.</p>
<p>--Fruits and nuts, $4.8 billion, up six percent.</p>
<p>--Vegetables, $3.85 billion, down seven percent.</p>
<p>--Cotton and linters, $3 billion, down 13 percent.</p>
<p>--Unmanufactured tobacco, $1.39 bilion, up five percent.</p>
<p>--Seeds and nursery, $948 million, up five percent.</p>
<p>--Total, $59.76 billion, up 10 percent.</p>
</text>
